ysics (CGS)\nSpecialized Literacy Studies (CGS)\nSustainable Enterprise (CGS)\nSustainable Family Enterprise (mCGS)\nTrauma-Response and Evidence-Based Practices (mCGS)\nAccelerated Master's Pathways (AMP), A to B\nAccountancy (AMP)\nAdvanced Specialties in Educational Practice (AMP)\nAgroecology (AMP)\nAnimal Biosciences (AMP)\nBiochemistry (AMP)\nBiology (AMP)\nBiomedical Engineering (AMP)\nBiostatistics (AMP)\nC to G\nChemistry (AMP)\nCivil and Environmental Engineering (AMP)\nCommunity Development and Applied Economics (AMP)\nComplex Systems and Data Science (AMP)\nComputer Science (AMP)\nCounseling (AMP)\nCurriculum and Instruction: Middle Level or Secondary Education (AMP)\nEducational Leadership and Policy Studies (AMP)\nElectrical Engineering (AMP)\nFood Systems (AMP)\nGreek and Latin (AMP)\nH to N\nHigher Education and Student Affairs Administration (AMP)\nHistoric Preservation (AMP)\nHistory (AMP)\nInterdisciplinary Educational Studies (AMP)\nLiterature, Theory, Media (AMP)\nMaterials Science (AMP)\nMathematical Sciences (AMP)\nMechanical Engineering (AMP)\nMedical Laboratory Science (AMP)\nMicrobiology and Molecular Genetics (AMP)\nNatural Resources (AMP)\nNursing (AMP)\nNutrition and Food Sciences (AMP)\nP to S\nPharmacology (AMP)\nPhysics (AMP)\nPsychology (AMP)\nPublic Administration (AMP)\nPublic Health (AMP)\nSpecial Education (AMP)\nStatistics (AMP)\nAdmissions Decisions\nThe policy of the Graduate College is that admission decisions must be finalized prior to the start of a semester (first day of classes in fall, spring, or summer session), and late admission decisions will not be approved retroactively. Applicants must submit all required materials well in advance of the semester in which they wish to matriculate, so that program faculty and chairs have suitable time to review materials and make admission recommendations to the Graduate College before the semester begins. Admission decisions made after the first day of classes in any semester will be for subsequent semesters.\nSome programs accept applications even after the usual application deadline, or on a rolling admissions basis, assuming sufficient program capacity. Admission decisions for these programs are subject to the same policy stated above. Contact the program to determine if they will accept a late application, and if time exists to complete the application process prior to the start of the semester.\nContact\nThe Graduate College\n85 South Prospect Street\n330 Waterman Building\nBurlington, VT 05405\ngraduate.admissions@uvm.edu\n(802) 656-2699\nExplore\nGraduate Admissions\nAcademic Programs\nGraduate Student Life\nAcademic Resources\nFaculty and Staff Resources\nOffice of Postdoctoral Affairs\nStrategic Plan\nGraduate College Team\nConnect\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nUniversity of Vermont home\nAccessibility\nPrivacy/Terms of Use", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.uvm.edu/graduate/academic-programs#main"], ["The Graduate College", "https://www.uvm.edu/group/76"], ["University of Vermont", "https://uvm.edu"], ["The Graduate College", "https://www.uvm.edu/graduate"], ["About", "https://www.uvm.edu/about-uvm"], ["Admissions", "https://www.uvm.edu/admissions"], ["Academics", "https://www.uvm.edu/academics"], ["Research", "https://www.uvm.edu/research"], ["Campus Life", "https://www.uvm.edu/campus-life"], ["Athletics", "https://www.uvm.edu/athletics-and-fitness"], ["Login to your UVM Dashboard", "https://myuvm.uvm.edu"], ["GIVE TO UVM", "https://www.uvmfoundation.org/s/1690/19/interior.aspx?sid=1690&gid=2&pgid=445&content_id=92"], ["VISIT UVM", "https://www.uvm.edu/admissions/undergraduate/visit-options"], ["Academic Calendar", "https://www.uvm.edu/registrar/uvm-academic-calendar"], ["Bookstore", "https://uvmbookstore.uvm.edu"], ["Commencement", "https://www.uvm.edu/commencement"], ["Parking and Transportation", "https://www.uvm.edu/transportation"], ["Summer University", "https://www.uvm.edu/summer"], ["UVM News", "https://ww